<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3073] Possible thread starvation due to rebalancing</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3073</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;We&apos;re currently rebalancing the utility cache in the system pool. This can cause starvation, for example in this scenario:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Start several nodes and a cache with indexing configured.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Continuously load the system with puts.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Add one more node. It will join and will start processing put requests immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;For each request, indexing processor will try to get binary metadata and will block on utility cache rebalance future. This will block all threads in the system pool.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Utility cache rebalancing will be scheduled but will never start, because all threads in system pool are blocked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;I think we should rebalance utility cache synchronously in exchange worker, like we do with the marshaller cache.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
